        "original_id": "f75e0909-00e6-59c7-a79e-1285cefeee39",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Garry Marshall, Leni Riefenstahl\n- Roles: actor, director, producer, writer, voice artist, screenwriter, editor, photographer, actress, dancer\n- Works: Happy Days, The Odd Couple, Pretty Woman, Runaway Bride, Valentine's Day, New Year's Eve, Mother's Day, The Princess Diaries\n\nFacts:\n- Garry Marshall was born on November 13, 1934, and died on July 19, 2016.\n- Garry Marshall was an American actor, director, producer, writer, and voice artist.\n- Garry Marshall was best known for creating Happy Days and its various spin-offs.\n- Garry Marshall developed Neil Simon's 1965 play The Odd Couple for television.\n- Garry Marshall directed Pretty Woman, Runaway Bride, Valentine's Day, New Year's Eve, Mother's Day, and The Princess Diaries.\n- Leni Riefenstahl was born on August 22, 1902, and died on September 8, 2003.\n- Leni Riefenstahl, born Helene Bertha Amalie Riefenstahl, was a German film director, producer, screenwriter, editor, photographer, actress, and dancer.",
